# L §5.19 example def, copied whole, with categories, spend_budget, the kind spending (its attribute category),
# spend_window and two statements completed.  "covered(x, span) is true when versions known by the cut cover place x
# on every day of the span ... A def that aggregates observations over a span must guard the aggregate with it ...
# Until a statement covers the window, the household's budget stands."  November is covered: learned = sum of
# -o.cash.amount over the food observations = -(234.22 + 100.00) = -334.22 PLN (the rent row is of category rent);
# with the window in December, not covered, the budget 1 000.00 PLN stands.  As written the def states no `at` and
# reads inputs whose rows all govern always: L §4.3 rule 2, it needs no law date.
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index categories = [food, rent]
input spend_budget[c in categories]: money PLN
input spend_window: key months
kind spending: transfers
  attr category: key categories
input bank: observed
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place landlord: outside lives 1900-01-01..

def spend_month[c in categories]: money PLN
  rule budget = spend_budget[c]
  rule learned beats budget = sum(-o.cash.amount for o in spending over spend_window where o.category == c) when covered(konto, spend_window)

version budget
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  spend_budget = 1 000.00 PLN
  spend_window = 2025-11

version statement_11
  cite s
  governs 2025-11
  known 2025-12-01
  covers konto
  anchor konto
  bank[r1] = (on: 2025-11-04, kind: spending, leg cash from konto to shop amount 234.22 PLN, category: food) "BIEDRONKA"
  bank[r2] = (on: 2025-11-12, kind: spending, leg cash from konto to shop amount 100.00 PLN, category: food) "LIDL"
  bank[r3] = (on: 2025-11-03, kind: spending, leg cash from konto to landlord amount 2 800.00 PLN, category: rent) "czynsz"

ask nov: spend_month[food] with spend_window = 2025-11
ask dec: spend_month[food] with spend_window = 2025-12
=== expect
dec: 1 000.00 PLN
  pinned: spend_window = 2025-12
  cut 2026-10-20
nov: -334.22 PLN
  pinned: spend_window = 2025-11
  cut 2026-10-20
